","wordFamily":["ad","advert","advertisable","advertisee","advertisement","advertiser","advertisey","advertising","it pays to advertise","nonadvertised","outadvertise","overadvertise","preadvertise","readvertise","self-advertise","spamvertise","unadvertised","underadvertisedadvertisable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advertise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:af668f7b93e3d13082","definition":"To notify (someone) of something; to call someone's attention to something.","example":"Socrates being advertiſed, that the God of wiſdome, had attributed the name of wiſe vnto him, was thereat much aſtoniſhed, and diligently ſearching and rouzing vp himſelf, and ranſaking the very ſecrets of his heart, found no foundation or ground for his divine ſentence.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["publish","promote","publicise","sell"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["ad","advert","advertisable","advertisee","advertisement","advertiser","advertisey","advertising","it pays to advertise","nonadvertised","outadvertise","overadvertise","preadvertise","readvertise","self-advertise","spamvertise","unadvertised","underadvertisedadvertisable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advertise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ab57f567eddb8c82f8","definition":"In gin rummy, to discard a card of one's preferred suit so as to mislead the opponent into thinking you do not want it.","example":"The safest time to answer a possible advertisement is when you have no indication as to what suit your opponent wants. Then even if he has advertised, the odds are that your answer is not the card he is looking for.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["publish","promote","publicise","sell"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage"